@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Trusted local deployment; explicit optional remote services
node "Trusted workstation (default setup)" <<device>> {
  node "Browser" as Browser <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "React/Vite frontend\nin-memory drafts/history" as React
    artifact "Browser speech APIs\nopt-in dictation / read-aloud" as Speech
  }
  node "Vite: development 5173\nor built preview 4173" as Vite <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "frontend source (development)\nor frontend/dist (preview)" as WebAssets
  }
  node "Python / FastAPI\nloopback:8000" as Backend <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "Backend + compiler" as Python
    artifact "Server-only .env / environment\nGEMINI_API_KEY" as Secret
  }
  node "Python / Tcl-Tk" as Tk <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "App.py + audio_utils.py" as Collector
  }
  node "Local storage" <<device>> {
    artifact "dataset.csv + cooperative lock" as CSV
    artifact "dictionary/camfranglais.md\n+ extra_lexicon.md (versioned)" as References
    artifact "audio / generated filenames" as Audio
    artifact "coursework / profile + PNGs" as Coursework
    artifact "User-chosen draft ZIP / snapshot\nreview before sharing" as Export
  }
  node "OS audio / default player" as OS <<executionEnvironment>>
}
node "Microphone / speakers" as Devices <<device>>
node "Gemini API" as Gemini <<external service>>
node "Browser-selected speech provider\nimplementation-dependent" as SpeechProvider <<external service>>
Browser -- Vite : local UI / assets HTTP
Vite -- Backend : configured /api proxy
Python ..> CSV : locked I/O
Python ..> References : read-only lookup
Python ..> Coursework : local I/O
Python ..> Export : download bytes
Collector ..> CSV : same lock protocol
Collector ..> Audio : WAV / copy
Tk -- OS : capture / play
OS -- Devices
Browser -- Devices : browser permissions
Backend -- Gemini : HTTPS; explicit AI requests
Browser -- SpeechProvider : may use online speech
Secret ..> Python
legend bottom
  No authentication or public multi-user deployment is supplied.
  CORS is not access control. Keep the backend on a trusted local boundary.
  If the backend is remote, its CSV/audio/profile live on that server.
  FastAPI exposes the API only; Vite serves development or built-preview UI.
  Production hosting needs a separate static server and matching API routing.
  AI/provider access is optional; local compiler, CRUD and exact reviewed lookup work offline.
endlegend
@enduml
